QBase

QBase is a modified version of ChartDB, an open source database diagram
editor (https://github.com/chartdb/chartdb). ChartDB is licensed under the GNU
Affero General Public License, version 3, and QBase is licensed under the
same terms: see LICENSE.

Copyright in the ChartDB code that QBase contains remains with its authors
and contributors; the history of the ChartDB repository lists them.

Changes made in QBase, from 14 October 2026:

- A backend (Node, Fastify, PostgreSQL, in server/) with accounts, projects,
  roles, an audit log, and optional two-factor sign-in.
- Published snapshots, read-only share links with live updates, schema lint
  and drift detection (shared/ and server/).
- Direct import from PostgreSQL and SQL Server, saved connections, re-sync.
- The editor works with the backend (src/lib/qubdi/, src/components/qubdi/).
- A new name, logo and look; the ChartDB name, images and links are removed.
